This file explains all of the variables in each of the datasets that accompany: Jennette, MA, Snodgrass, JW, Forester, DC. 2018ms. Variation in age, body size, and reproductive traits among urban and rural amphibian populations\
\
dataset: FrogAgeReduce.csv (this dataset is reduced as young and old age classes were combined to eliminate structural zeros from the data matrix)\
Sex         =   indicates the sex of wood frog\
Age         =   estimated age of wood frogs based on skeletal chronology\
weight      =   number of individuals represented by the combination of sex, age, and population; weight in the sense of a count\
pop         =   wood frog population of origin\
\
dataset: ToadAgeReduce.csv (this dataset is reduced as young and old age classes were combined to eliminate structural zeros from the data matrix)\
Sex         =   indicates the sex of American toads\
Age         =   estimated age of American toads based on skeletal chronology\
weight      =   number of individuals represented by the combination of sex, age, and population; weight in the sense of a count\
pop         =   American toads population of origin\
\
dataset: femalestoadage.csv\
POP         =   Population of origin for female American toads; 2 = Urban C , 3 = Urban B, 4 = Urban A, 5= Suburban A, 6 = Rural\
Weight      =   somatic dry weight   \
SVL         =   south vent length in mm \
Age         =   estimated age of American toads based on skeletal chronology\
\
dataset: Malestoadage.csv\
POP         =   Population of origin for male American toads;2 = Urban C , 3 = Urban B, 4 = Urban A, 5= Suburban A, 6 = Rural\
Weight      =   somatic dry weight in mg   \
SVL         =   south vent length in mm \
Age         =   estimated age of male American toads based on skeletal chronology\
\
dataset: femaleswoodage.csv\
POP         =   Population of origin for female wood frogs; RUR.A = Rural A, RUR.B = Rural B, SUB.A = Suburban A, URB.D = Urban\
Weight      =   somatic dry weight in mg   \
SVL         =   south vent length in mm \
Age         =   estimated age of American toads based on skeletal chronology\
